# Python Port Plan — Step 11_tui

## Goal

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/11_tui` (a full terminal UI wrapping the REPL:
scrollable conversation viewport, live progress line, input box, status
line, driven by the `charm` gem's bubbletea/lipgloss/bubbles bindings) to
Python at `week1_baseline/python/11_tui`.

**This is not a literal architectural mirror**, unlike every step 00-10.
Ruby's TUI is built on `charm`, a native-extension binding to Go's Bubble
Tea/Lip Gloss/Bubbles libraries (see `week1_baseline/ruby/11_tui/patches/bubbletea/` --
real C source patching a Go-runtime input conflict). There is no Python
equivalent to bind to. The port instead uses **Textual** (PyPI `textual`,
currently 6.5.0, stable/actively maintained -- verified 2026-07-24, not
assumed), replicating the *behavior* (four-zone layout, live progress
during a turn, keyboard shortcuts, background-thread agent execution)
using Textual's own idioms rather than mirroring bubbletea's Elm-style
`init`/`update`/`view` architecture line-by-line. Same category of
decision as `09_global_executable` (not every step ports 1:1) -- named
explicitly here rather than silently assumed.

